load-launch-profiles-from-config

Lane: backend

Unit: select-launch-arguments-by-symlink

ChildPatch: load-launch-profiles-from-config

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Select configured literal launch arguments by the invoked CLI symlink name while allowing explicit arguments to override profile defaults.

Requires: none

Provides: Read named string arrays from home config.toml symlinks, initialize absent profiles with codex and codex-embedded defaults through native config edits, expand only actual symlink invocations, and report invalid configuration or missing names without shell parsing.

Boundary: Direct executable invocation does not read or create profiles; native CLI parsing, configuration precedence after argument expansion, process roots, and daemon lifecycle remain with their existing owners.

Verification: cli symlink_launch_tests cover default creation, preservation of unrelated settings, literal arguments, explicit overrides, direct-executable bypass, and observable errors; current config schema describes symlinks as arrays of strings.


